    <node id="Paper_866">
      <data key="d0">Paper</data>
      <data key="d1">Vis</data>
      <data key="d2">1993</data>
      <data key="d3">GRASPARC-A problem solving environment integrating computation and visualization</data>
      <data key="d4">10.1109/visual.1993.398857</data>
      <data key="d5">http://dx.doi.org/10.1109/VISUAL.1993.398857</data>
      <data key="d6">102.0</data>
      <data key="d7">109.0</data>
      <data key="d8">C</data>
      <data key="d9">Visualization has proved an efficient tool in the understanding of large data sets in computational science and engineering. There is growing interest today in the development of problem solving environments which integrate both visualization and the computational process which generates the data. The GRASPARC project has looked at some of the issues involved in creating such an environment. An architecture is proposed in which tools for computation and visualization can be embedded in a framework which assists in the management of the problem solving process. This framework has an integral data management facility which allows an audit trail of the experiments to be recorded. This design therefore allows not only steering but also backtracking and more complicated problem solving strategies. A number of demonstrator case studies have been implemented.&amp;lt;&amp;lt;ETX&amp;gt;&amp;gt;</data>
      <data key="d10">Ken Brodlie;Andrew Poon;Helen Wright;Lesley Brankin;Greg Banecki;Alan Gay</data>
      <data key="d11">K. Brodlie;A. Poon;H. Wright;L. Brankin;G. Banecki;A. Gay</data>
      <data key="d12">School of Computer Studies, University of Leeds, Leeds, UK;School of Computer Studies, University of Leeds, Leeds, UK;School of Computer Studies, University of Leeds, Leeds, UK;NAG Limited, Oxford, UK;NAG Limited, Oxford, UK;NAG Limited, Oxford, UK</data>
      <data key="d13">10.1109/visual.1992.235219;10.1109/visual.1991.175818;10.1109/visual.1992.235219</data>
      <data key="d14" />
      <data key="d15">149.0</data>
      <data key="d16">40.0</data>
      <data key="d17">15.0</data>
      <data key="d18">213.0</data>
      <data key="d19" />
      <data key="d20" />
    </node>
    <node id="Author_Ken Brodlie">
      <data key="d0">Author</data>
      <data key="d21">Ken Brodlie</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Author_Andrew Poon">
      <data key="d0">Author</data>
      <data key="d21">Andrew Poon</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Author_Helen Wright">
      <data key="d0">Author</data>
      <data key="d21">Helen Wright</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Author_Lesley Brankin">
      <data key="d0">Author</data>
      <data key="d21">Lesley Brankin</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Author_Greg Banecki">
      <data key="d0">Author</data>
      <data key="d21">Greg Banecki</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Author_Alan Gay">
      <data key="d0">Author</data>
      <data key="d21">Alan Gay</data>
