    <node id="Paper_1047">
      <data key="d0">Paper</data>
      <data key="d1">Vis</data>
      <data key="d2">1990</data>
      <data key="d3">FAST: a multi-processed environment for visualization of computational fluid dynamics</data>
      <data key="d4">10.1109/visual.1990.146360</data>
      <data key="d5">http://dx.doi.org/10.1109/VISUAL.1990.146360</data>
      <data key="d6">14.0</data>
      <data key="d7" />
      <data key="d8">C</data>
      <data key="d9">The authors discuss FAST (flow analysis software toolkit), an implementation of a software system for fluid mechanics analysis. Visualization of computational aerodynamics requires flexible, extensible, and adaptable software tools for performing analysis tasks. An overview of FAST is given, and its architecture is discussed. Interactive visualization control is addressed. The advantages and disadvantages of FAST are discussed.&amp;lt;&amp;lt;ETX&amp;gt;&amp;gt;</data>
      <data key="d10">Gordon V. Bancroft;Fergus Merritt;Todd Plessel;Paul G. Kelaita;R. Kevin McCabe;Al Globus</data>
      <data key="d11">G.V. Bancroft;F.J. Merritt;T.C. Plessel;P.G. Kelaita;R.K. McCabe;A. Globus</data>
      <data key="d12">Sterling Federal Systems, Inc., Palo Alto, CA, USA;Sterling Federal Systems, Inc., Palo Alto, CA, USA;Sterling Federal Systems, Inc., Palo Alto, CA, USA;Sterling Federal Systems, Inc., Palo Alto, CA, USA;Sterling Federal Systems, Inc., Palo Alto, CA, USA;Sterling Federal Systems, Inc., Palo Alto, CA, USA</data>
      <data key="d13" />
      <data key="d14" />
      <data key="d15">152.0</data>
      <data key="d16">34.0</data>
      <data key="d17">20.0</data>
      <data key="d18">177.0</data>
