    <node id="Paper_1862">
      <data key="d0">Paper</data>
      <data key="d1">VAST</data>
      <data key="d2">2007</data>
      <data key="d3">Thin Client Visualization</data>
      <data key="d4">10.1109/vast.2007.4388996</data>
      <data key="d5">http://dx.doi.org/10.1109/VAST.2007.4388996</data>
      <data key="d6">51.0</data>
      <data key="d7">58.0</data>
      <data key="d8">C</data>
      <data key="d9">We have developed a Web 2.0 thin client visualization framework called GeoBoosttrade. Our framework focuses on geospatial visualization and using scalable vector graphics (SVG), AJAX, RSS and GeoRSS we have built a complete thin client component set. Our component set provides a rich user experience that is completely browser based. It includes maps, standard business charts, graphs, and time-oriented components. The components are live, interactive, linked, and support real time collaboration.</data>
      <data key="d10">Stephen G. Eick;M. Andrew Eick;Jesse Fugitt;Brian Horst;Maxim Khailo;Russell A. Lankenau</data>
      <data key="d11">Stephen G. Eick;M. Andrew Eick;Jesse Fugitt;Brian Horst;Maxim Khailo;Russell A. Lankenau</data>
      <data key="d12">SSS Research, Inc., Naperville, IL, USA;SSS Research, Inc., Naperville, IL, USA;SSS Research, Inc., Naperville, IL, USA;SSS Research, Inc., Naperville, IL, USA;SSS Research, Inc., Naperville, IL, USA;SSS Research, Inc., Naperville, IL, USA</data>
      <data key="d13" />
      <data key="d14">web 20, JavaScript, scalable vector graphics, visualization components, linked view visual analytics</data>
      <data key="d15">16.0</data>
      <data key="d16">16.0</data>
      <data key="d17">9.0</data>
      <data key="d18">380.0</data>
