    <node id="Paper_2403">
      <data key="d0">Paper</data>
      <data key="d1">InfoVis</data>
      <data key="d2">2019</data>
      <data key="d3">Winglets: Visualizing Association with Uncertainty in Multi-class Scatterplots</data>
      <data key="d4">10.1109/tvcg.2019.2934811</data>
      <data key="d5">http://dx.doi.org/10.1109/TVCG.2019.2934811</data>
      <data key="d6">770.0</data>
      <data key="d7">779.0</data>
      <data key="d8">J</data>
      <data key="d9">This work proposes Winglets, an enhancement to the classic scatterplot to better perceptually pronounce multiple classes by improving the perception of association and uncertainty of points to their related cluster. Designed as a pair of dual-sided strokes belonging to a data point, Winglets leverage the Gestalt principle of Closure to shape the perception of the form of the clusters, rather than use an explicit divisive encoding. Through a subtle design of two dominant attributes, length and orientation, Winglets enable viewers to perform a mental completion of the clusters. A controlled user study was conducted to examine the efficiency of Winglets in perceiving the cluster association and the uncertainty of certain points. The results show Winglets form a more prominent association of points into clusters and improve the perception of associating uncertainty.</data>
      <data key="d10">Min Lu 0002;Shuaiqi Wang;Joel Lanir;Noa Fish;Yang Yue 0001;Daniel Cohen-Or;Hui Huang 0004</data>
      <data key="d11">Min Lu;Shuaiqi Wang;Joel Lanir;Noa Fish;Yang Yue;Daniel Cohen-Or;Hui Huang</data>
      <data key="d12">Shenzhen University;Shenzhen University;University of Haifa;Tel Aviv Univeristy;Shenzhen University;Shenzhen University;Shenzhen University</data>
      <data key="d13">10.1109/vast.2010.5652460;10.1109/tvcg.2014.2346594;10.1109/tvcg.2009.122;10.1109/tvcg.2013.183;10.1109/tvcg.2018.2865141;10.1109/tvcg.2018.2865141;10.1109/tvcg.2017.2744184;10.1109/tvcg.2013.153;10.1109/vast.2009.5332628;10.1109/tvcg.2018.2864912;10.1109/vast.2010.5652460</data>
      <data key="d14">Scatterplot,Gestalt laws,Association,Uncertainty</data>
      <data key="d15">16.0</data>
      <data key="d16">9.0</data>
      <data key="d17">43.0</data>
      <data key="d18">909.0</data>
      <data key="d19" />
      <data key="d20" />
    </node>
    <node id="Author_Shuaiqi Wang">
      <data key="d0">Author</data>
      <data key="d21">Shuaiqi Wang</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Author_Noa Fish">
      <data key="d0">Author</data>
      <data key="d21">Noa Fish</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Author_Yang Yue 0001">
      <data key="d0">Author</data>
      <data key="d21">Yang Yue 0001</data>
